        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_20c22e9f2ae745bfabafa57c9553fdf0",
      "statement": "On create/update, every requested environment member is resolved through the SCM provider concurrently so persisted rows carry the resolved repo_id and the request branch or the freshly resolved default branch; the first resolution failure in input order wins deterministically.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://packages/control-plane/src/routes/environments.ts#L70-L92",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:47151c861ec86330a913dba4b75b3dafa9066ab2962e925766ec238a9d875daf:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_73d7ff2d57ed4141a6064e43b33540b5",
      "statement": "resolveEnvironmentTarget is the control-plane entrypoint for launching from an environment: it raises 404 when the environment does not exist and 500 on an empty member set (a data-integrity fault, since the schema requires at least one member), and hands the snapshot to resolveSessionRepositories so an environment session gets the same all-or-nothing SCM check as an ad-hoc list — a member whose access was revoked after creation fails the create rather than booting a partial workspace.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://packages/control-plane/src/repos/resolve.ts#L28-L48",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:0b51e7b10758fc53f0331b726dd5715b3a172433663298a649203c21f323eaf9:"
        },
        {
