    {
      "id": "claim_cee5d749f08149dab467715ebe2d58b7",
      "statement": "Before selecting an environment, the GitHub bot extends caller gating across the whole member set: an explicit allowedTriggerUsers allowlist vouches for the sender without GitHub permission checks, otherwise the sender needs write permission on every environment repository — an environment launch must not widen what the sender can reach beyond what GitHub already grants them.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://packages/github-bot/src/session-target.ts#L130-L179",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:af30b4e0b6337c0adff75fc8e7a5addf60de41e9dcca62768e0d1582db84ba8a:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_e4e3d0bee63a409c9989853bd0adf4ff",
      "statement": "Prebuild scheduling is write-side: saving a prebuild-enabled environment (create or update) fires a detached best-effort rebuild via scheduleImageBuildOnSave, and any environment secrets mutation synchronously supersedes every live image whose baked secrets are now outdated before the response returns — a supersede failure surfaces as a distinct 500 asking the caller to retry, so revoked values never stay baked in a selectable image.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://packages/control-plane/src/image-builds/save-hooks.ts#L28-L63",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:a271cc60e82711ed33cb51bbd5144ed0375dda8dcfd1d1de9bd0b3d5b99f5bc7:"
