    {
      "id": "claim_efb0b568a5fc4611ad5021a2f2aad399",
      "statement": "Environment-level integration settings are the top layer of the integration-settings resolution chain — global defaults, then per-repo overrides, then environment overrides, with later layers winning and undefined keys never clobbering — and only the session-scoped integrations (sandbox, code-server, vnc) accept this level; sessions resolve settings once at create time so later edits never affect running sessions, while the enabledRepos allowlist stays evaluated against the repo.",
