    {
      "id": "claim_4b5509b95b0644919acd222f79deb221",
      "statement": "The Slack and Linear bots treat environments as first-class session targets alongside repositories: environment ids are encoded as env:<id> select values, rules and channel associations resolve them against a cached environment list that fails open to empty (rules targeting a deleted or unfetchable environment are skipped), and branch preferences never apply because the environment defines its own branches.",
